;;; derivative, the argument principle, Rouche's theorem and the counting of solutions.
;;;   (1)  cc-open-minus-finite(-induction)   an open set minus a finite subset of CC is open
;;;   (2)  cc-power-sub-diff                  d/dz (z - c)^(j+1) = (j+1)(z - c)^j, j symbolic
;;;   (3)  log-derivative-at-pole             Prop 4.17, pole case: f'/f = h - N/(z - c) near a pole of order N
;;;   (4)  simple-pole-of-decomposition       fn = h + d/(z - c), d /= 0: a pole of order 1 with residue d
;;;   (5)  log-derivative-residue-at-pole / -at-zero   Prop 4.17: f'/f has a pole of order 1, residue -N / m
;;;   (6)  pole-order-unique, pole-order-value          the order of a pole (POLE-ORDER, ch4d-vocab.scm)
;;;   (7)  argument-principle                 Prop 4.19 for f meromorphic: zeros and poles, the degree sum
;;;   (8)  road-holomorphic-composite, winding-unfold-eq, winding-of-composite   f o gamma and ind(f o gamma, w)
;;;   (12) convex-closed-path-null-homotopic  a closed path in a convex open set is null-homotopic there
;;;   (13) zero-order-restrict                the order of a zero is local
;;;   (9)  zeros-poles-finite                 Z u P is a finite subset of u
;;;   (10) rouche-theorem                     Prop 4.20 (meromorphic f, g)
;;;   (11) meromorphic-at-sum / -product / -recip   Prop 4.12 at a point (Example 4.8 for the reciprocal)
;;;   (15) holomorphic-is-meromorphic-at, meromorphic-on-sum / -product   Prop 4.12 on U: sums and products
;;;   (14) zeros-count-winding                Prop 4.24: solutions of f = w in a disc = ind(f o gamma, w)
;;;   (16) finsum-one-card-induction          the sum of ones over a finite subset of CC is its cardinality
;;;   (17) simple-zero-order-one              Remark 4.23: f(b) = 0, f'(b) /= 0 => a zero of order 1
;;;   (18) circle-trace-of-magnitude          |y - c| = r puts y on the trace of the circle path
;;;   (19) multiplicity-local-simple          near a point of multiplicity n: f /= f(a), f' /= 0
;;;   (20) local-n-to-one                     Theorem 4.25: every value near w taken exactly n times near a
