;;; ===============================================================================================================
;;; (20) THEOREM 4.25: f holomorphic on a connected open u, f(a) = w with multiplicity n >= 1.  Then there are open
;;;      V inside u containing a and W with f(V) = W, and every z in W other than w has exactly n preimages in V.
;;;      gamma = the circle of radius r about a (r half the radius of (19)); W = a ball about w on which
;;;      ind(f o gamma, .) is constant (winding-locally-constant); by 4.24 that constant counts the solutions with
;;;      multiplicity, = n at w (the only solution is a); off w every solution is simple (Remark 4.23), so the count
;;;      is the cardinality.  V = the points of B(a, r) that f sends into W.
;;; ===============================================================================================================
